{
  "The rules every control follows: Tab order, the active control of a container, focus that never falls to `<body>`, `&File` access keys and app-wide shortcuts.": "",
  "Every control is a Tab stop unless `tabStop = false`; `tabIndex` orders the controls of a container.": "",
  "Containers (`FocusContainer`) track `activeControl` and put focus back with `restoreFocus()` when they become active again.": "",
  "One Tab stop, arrow keys inside (roving tabindex or `aria-activedescendant`): with the first composite control.": "",
  "Disabling, hiding, removing or disposing the focused part of a control moves focus to the next usable element.": "",
  "Only for keyboard use (`:focus-visible`), the design system's double ring.": "",
  "`&Save` in a control text: Alt+S. Underlined while Alt is held.": "",
  "`addShortcut('Ctrl+S', …)` app-wide, or scoped to a control.": "",
  "Tab order": "",
  "Give controls a `tabIndex` and the outermost container of the page or window visits them in ascending order at each level of the control tree; equal indexes (and plain elements, index 0) go in document order. Until a control inside sets a `tabIndex`, Tab is left to the browser. A modal window keeps Tab inside itself; one radio button per group is a stop, as in browsers.": "",
  "Active control": "",
  "A `FocusContainer` knows which control inside holds focus (`activeControl`, reactive) and puts focus back there with `restoreFocus()`: a window coming to the front, a tab page coming back.": "",
  "Access keys": "",
  "`&` before a letter: `&Save`, `Save &as…`. `&&` is a literal ampersand. Only the first marker counts.": "",
  "Alt + the key; on Apple platforms Control + Option + the key, because Option alone types characters there (browsers use the same keys for HTML `accesskey`).": "",
  "The key activates the control: a button is focused and clicked (as HTML `accesskey` does), another control is focused (`onAccessKey()`).": "",
  "Each press moves focus to the next one, activating none.": "",
  "The modal window while one is open, else the window holding focus, else the page outside windows. Disabled and hidden controls are skipped.": "",
  "Ignored: AltGr (Ctrl+Alt on Windows) types characters such as `@` on a Turkish keyboard.": "",
  "Shown while Alt is held (Control + Option on Apple platforms). Tapping Alt (press and release) keeps it shown until Alt is tapped again, another key is pressed or the pointer is used; while the page has access keys, that tap is kept from the browser, which would otherwise move keyboard focus to its menu bar. `data-mx-access-keys=\"always\"` on `<html>` shows it all the time.": "",
  "The accessible name is the plain text; the control gets `aria-keyshortcuts=\"Alt+S\"` (`\"Control+Alt+S\"` on Apple platforms).": "",
  "Any element with `aria-keyshortcuts=\"Alt+N\"` takes part: a button-like one is clicked, an input focused, a `<label>` focuses its field.": "",
  "Browsers keep a few Alt combinations for their own menus, and they differ per browser and language; test the keys you choose.": "",
  "Shortcuts": "",
  "Chords": "",
  "Meaning": "",
  "The Ctrl key.": "",
  "The Alt key (Option on a Mac).": "",
  "The Shift key.": "",
  "The Windows key, Cmd on a Mac.": "",
  "Cmd on Apple platforms, Ctrl elsewhere: `Mod+S` saves everywhere.": "",
  "A character (`S`, `1`, `/`), or a `KeyboardEvent.key` name: `Enter`, `Escape` (`Esc`), `Delete` (`Del`), `F2`, `ArrowUp` (`Up`), `Space`, `Plus`… Case does not matter; `Ctrl++` is Ctrl and plus.": "",
  "Which shortcut runs": "",
  "Shortcuts scoped to the controls holding focus run first, the innermost one first; app-wide ones last. A handler that returns `false` passes the key on.": "",
  "While a modal window is open, only shortcuts scoped inside it run; app-wide ones are silent.": "",
  "App-wide shortcuts without Ctrl, Alt or Meta (Delete, Escape, a letter) do not run while focus is in a window: those keys belong to the window. Chords with a modifier and F-keys still do.": "",
  "A chord without Ctrl, Alt or Meta leaves text fields alone (Delete deletes text) unless `inEditable: true`. F-keys and chords with a modifier work everywhere.": "",
  "A shortcut scoped to a disabled control does not run.": "",
  "The key gets `preventDefault()` and stops there. Shortcuts run before access keys: an explicit chord wins over an implicit key.": "",
  "Focus never on &lt;body&gt;": "",
  "When the focused part of a control is disabled, hidden, removed (a list row, a branch) or disposed, focus moves to the next usable element from that spot in the same window, else the one before it. A click on an empty spot still clears focus as usual, and route changes are left to the router.": "",
  "Returns / kind": "",
  "Registers a shortcut; returns the remover. `options.scope`: a component; `options.inEditable`: also in text fields.": "",
  "The same, scoped to the control and removed when it is disposed.": "",
  "Parses `&Text` for your own controls; render with the `mx-access-key` class and call `setAccessKey(key)`.": "",
  "prop / property": "",
  "Order inside the container; default 0.": "",
  "See the Control page.": "",
  "Controls: see `Control` for `tabStop`, `tabIndex`, `focus()`, `onAccessKey()` and `FocusContainer`.": ""
}
